  {
    "id": "anno-toyoura_upper_p056_left-07",
    "type": "Annotation",
    "body": [
      {
        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "人口四千四百八十七人內"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "人口　四千四百八十七人　内"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Rear-vassal (baisotsu) population as printed: 4,487 persons. The printed figure is wrong, and two independent checks show what it should be. First, the two sub-counts below give 750 male and 737 female, which add to 1,487. Second, the facing leaf (printed page 86) states 1,931 samurai-and-sotsu households holding 8,665 people; subtract the three other components (士族 426 households / 2,121 people, 准士 301 / 1,456, 卒 779 / 3,601) and exactly 425 households and 1,487 people remain for the rear vassals, matching the household figure this page prints. The total was re-read at eight-times single-character magnification: the third glyph is 四 and the fourth is 千 with its slanted top stroke, so the page really does print 四千四百八十七. The transcription and the parsed value therefore keep what the page shows, and agree with MASTER; the true figure is 1,487, and the compositor appears to have set an extra 四 before 千."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "陪卒人口"
      }
    ],
    "target": {
      "source": "images/upper_p056_left.jpg",
      "selector": {
