      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "（一二八"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Opening of the bracketed small-type note attached to the temple count. Three glyphs stand below the bracket arc, each centred on the column axis and set at warichu size (measured widths 47, 35 and 37 pixels against 63 to 66 for the main-column glyphs), and they read 一, 二, 八 — on the face of it the figure 128. They occupy the place where this survey usually prints a single centred 內 marker; the neighbouring entry on printed page 85 opens its temple bracket that way. Here no unit and no label follows them, and 128 reconciles with none of the figures in the note: neither the 373 sites above, nor the 164 establishments below, nor the population of 1,037. Recorded verbatim, because the page does not say what the number counts."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "寺割註一二八"
      }
    ],
